--- a/.andromeda/test-plan.md
+++ b/.andromeda/test-plan.md
@@ -548,2 +548,3 @@
 decision/fake-agent-matches-recordings · Fake agent matches recordings byte for byte — For each recorded fixture set, walked at run time, the fake agent's hook sequence and payloads equal the recorded order and bytes, never an insta snapshot; an empty walk fails.
+decision/fired-wake-keeps-wheel · A fired scheduled wake keeps the driver's wheel — A keyless human-filed prompt-submitted is relabelled origin harness with no wheel move when no stdin key set the typed mark, the last turn end counted at least one scheduled wake and the CLI is verified; otherwise it takes the human wheel. · guard: path5_a_fired_wake_keeps_the_driver_wheel_its_next_send_and_its_dialog
 decision/fixtures-match-tolerant-schema · Fixtures checked against the tolerant schema — jsonschema checks every recorded fixture against the tolerant parser schema: unknown fields allowed, closed enums required.
@@ -566,3 +567,3 @@
 decision/live-failing-reading-not-verification · Live reading recorded as read, never as verification — A live reading that fails a ledger row is recorded as read and never as verification of the row; a confounded live reading leaves the row unverified on that CLI version and its live re-read owed.
-decision/live-rig-hint-cell-reading · Live rig hint-cell reading recorded as a reading — The live rig's hint-cell reading records the attribute words of every drawn hint cell past the cursor cell after the second send, as a reading and never as verification; no drawn cell reads unread (no-cell).
+decision/live-rig-hint-cell-reading · Live rig hint-cell reading recorded as a reading — The live rig's hint-cell reading records the attribute words of every drawn hint cell past the cursor cell, after the second send or in a fresh box before any send, as a reading and never as verification; no drawn cell reads unread (no-cell).
 decision/mcp-stdio-test-owns-child · MCP stdio test owns the child — MCP stdio tests run an rmcp client over a viola mcp child the test spawns and owns, closing its stdin and awaiting its exit, never rmcp's TokioChildProcess, beside a replay of the recorded MCP exchange.
@@ -575,2 +576,3 @@
 decision/property-tests-on-parsers · Property tests on every parser surface — proptest at 512 cases covers every parser surface: paste validation, ndjson framing at the frame cap plus and minus one, the hook stdin, agents and hyprctl reply parsers, the vt100 feed and prompt-submitted normalisation, with its regressions directory committed.
+decision/rig-no-key-read-from-keys-word · Rig rehearsal reads no key typed from its own keys word — A live rig rehearsal reads no key typed from the rig's own keys word, never from the fake-agent receipt. · why: The shared receipt carries viola send's submit Enters as key lines.
 decision/scan-hits-never-echo-bytes · Scan hits never echo bytes — A secret-scan hit is reported by place and class, never by the matched bytes.
@@ -843,2 +845,3 @@
 contract/fake-agent-cli/start-screen · viola-fake-agent command line · --start-screen — Under --screens, a trusted start given --start-screen <phase> draws Screen.<phase> in place of its ready screen and keeps it standing; each stdin byte is one key receipt line, Ctrl-C ends it with no key line, and no byte reaches the input box.
+contract/fake-agent-cli/stop-crons · viola-fake-agent command line · --stop-crons — The argv-only --stop-crons <n>, 0 to 4, puts n synthetic elements in every Stop's session_crons.
