@@ -848,2 +851,3 @@
 contract/fake-agent-cli/unknown-arguments · viola-fake-agent command line · unknown arguments — Unknown arguments are ignored.
+contract/fake-agent-cli/wake-after-ms · viola-fake-agent command line · --wake-after-ms — The argv-only --wake-after-ms <ms>, capped at 5 000, fires once, that long after the first Stop carrying a non-empty session_crons, a keyless recorded UserPromptSubmit, and under --turn-stop its turn end.
 contract/fake-agent-events/session-start · viola-fake-agent fired events · SessionStart — After start_receipts the fake agent fires SessionStart (variant default) once, silent without a registered hook or a fixture, like every fire; under --screens with an untrusted cwd only after Enter on the trust row, which draws the ready screen.
@@ -851,3 +855,3 @@
 contract/fake-agent-hooks/command-spawn · viola-fake-agent hook execution · hook command — The fake agent reads the hook commands from the plugin dir run passes and runs every command entry for the event; an absolute command is spawned directly, never through a shell or a PATH lookup, and a non-absolute one is never run.
-contract/fake-agent-hooks/stdin-payload · viola-fake-agent hook execution · hook stdin payload — The payload on a hook's stdin is the recorded fixture's bytes, save the fields a prompt, a resume, a compact replay or the launch SessionStart under --transcript sets.
